WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.220
A secure CMake roadmap begins with clarity.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:09.960
Use target-based design so settings are close to the libraries, executables, tests, and tools they affect.

3
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.300
Avoid unnecessary global state.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:19.840
Scope public, private, and interface properties deliberately so downstream users inherit only what they should.

5
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.620
Structure the project so build boundaries are visible to reviewers.

6
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.180
Next, make safe configurations easy to use.

7
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.760
Define approved presets, documented options, and clear build profiles.

8
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:38.660
Centralize compiler, linker, warning, sanitizer, and hardening policy in reviewable CMake logic.

9
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.320
Make unsupported combinations fail early.

10
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:46.700
Confirm through logs and artifact checks that release builds received the intended settings.

11
00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.540
Then control the inputs and outputs.

12
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.480
Pin and review dependencies.

13
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:57.100
Document toolchains, sysroots, SDKs, cache variables, and environment assumptions.

14
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:03.680
Treat generated code, custom commands, and build-time scripts as security-relevant work.

15
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:12.500
Review install rules, RPATH behavior, package metadata, debug artifacts, and final archive contents before delivery.

16
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.100
Finally, make governance routine.

17
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:22.400
CI should exercise approved profiles, inspect artifacts, preserve evidence, and report drift as a defect.

18
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:29.380
CMake changes should receive the same seriousness as source changes because they can alter what ships.

19
00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:36.520
Build security is application security: it connects the code the team wrote to the binary the user receives.
